  "notes": "WRITING:\nThe kanji {曖昧|あいまい} uses rare characters and is often written in hiragana.\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nJapanese communication is often described as {曖昧|あいまい} by non-Japanese speakers. This can be intentional to maintain harmony ({和|わ}) or leave room for interpretation.\n\nUSAGE:\n- {曖昧|あいまい}な⟦{態度|たいど}→態度：03396_taido⟧ (ambiguous attitude)\n- {曖昧|あいまい}⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ (to make ambiguous, to be evasive)\n- {曖昧|あいまい}さ (ambiguity - noun form)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {曖昧|あいまい}: neutral term for ambiguity\n- ⟦うやむや→うやむや：08049_uyamuya⟧: deliberately obscured\n- ⟦あやふや→あやふや：08050_ayafuya⟧: unreliable or poorly defined",
